# Remnawave Host values: Beget CDN

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Remark | Beget CDN |
| Address | `${BEGET_HOST_DOMAIN}` |
| Port | `443` |
| Config Profile | `${CONFIG_PROFILE_NAME}` |
| Inbound | `${BEGET_XRAY_INBOUND_TAG}` |
| Network | `xhttp` |
| Security Layer | `TLS` |
| SNI | `${BEGET_HOST_DOMAIN}` |
| Host | `${BEGET_HOST_DOMAIN}` |
| Path | `${BEGET_XHTTP_PATH}` |
| Mode | `packet-up` |
| ALPN | `h2,http/1.1` |
| Fingerprint | `chrome` |
| Allow insecure | `OFF` |
| Flow | empty |
| Internal Squad | `${BEGET_SQUAD_NAME}` |

Use `remnawave-xhttp-extra.json` from the same build directory. Set Path separately
to `${BEGET_XHTTP_PATH}` with no trailing slash. Keep these settings identical
on the client and server:

- `uplinkHTTPMethod: GET`;
- `sessionIdPlacement: query`, `sessionIdKey: x_session`;
- `seqPlacement: query`, `seqKey: x_seq`;
- `xPaddingPlacement: header`, `xPaddingHeader: X-Cache`, `xPaddingMethod: tokenish`.

Do not use `queryInHeader`: it puts a full URL in `X-Cache`, which returned CDN
403 responses in integration tests. After updating the inbound and Host Extra,
refresh the client subscription and check the exported client configuration.
